      "description": "Watch Levante vs Barcelona highlights and goals from La Liga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 13, 2026. On September 13, 2026, Levante hosted Barcelona in a La Liga clash that delivered high-octane drama and a rollercoaster of emotions. The match served as a showcase for tactical adjustments and individual brilliance, keeping the spectators engaged from start to finish. Barcelona's Early Dominance Barcelona wasted no time establishing control, taking the lead just five minutes into the match. Xavi Espart unleashed a precise strike from outside the box following a setup by Raphinha , leaving the home defense stunned. The pressure remained relentless, and in the 19th minute, Lamine Yamal doubled the advantage with a clinical left-footed finish. The goal was the result of a fluid move involving Fermin Lopez and another assist from the creative Raphinha . As the first half drew to a close, the intensity spiked with yellow cards shown to Gerard Martin and Hugo Sotelo . Despite Levante 's efforts to disrupt the rhythm, Barcelona maintained a staggering 74% possession, dictating the tempo and restricting the hosts to sporadic counter-attacks that rarely threatened Joan Garcia ’s goal. A Late Surge and the Decisive Blow The second half began with Barcelona further tightening their grip on the game. In the 48th minute, Lamine Yamal was fouled in the area by Aissa Mandi and subsequently converted the penalty, despite Mathew Ryan getting a hand to it. At 0-3, the result seemed a formality, but Levante staged a spirited comeback late in the game. Ivan Romero capitalized on a defensive lapse in the 79th minute, and Roger Brugue made it 2-3 in the 88th minute, setting up a frantic finale. In the dying moments of stoppage time, Barcelona finally put the game to bed. In the 93rd minute, Karim Adeyemi scored with a composed right-footed shot after being played through by Marc Bernal . This goal extinguished Levante 's hopes of a miracle comeback and confirmed a deserved, albeit hard-fought, victory for the visitors."
